One problem is that you know these particular bones files because 
you've explored them before; but of course, they're *your* bones files,
and you'd know what's there anyway -- especially the bones pile that
includes the cursed +3 SDSM in a spiked pit, that hurt a lot and
you remember it very distinctly -- but when you've explored it 
before, you may also remember which items were cursed. If you're like
me, you won't remember most of what's in them.

Another problem is that you are increasing the probability of getting 
a bones file above the "natural" probability. Why people think it's
okay to do this with hearse but not okay to do it with your own boneses,
that's a mystery.

So it seems to me that if you're not restoring special boneses like the
cursed +3 sdsm, and if you're not restoring bones files where you 
remember too much about the situation, perhaps no real harm is done.

But it is a bit iffy.

